 #### Incremental Chunk Re-meshing
 - **Definition**: A technique to keep deformation fast and seamless by only re-meshing chunks affected by edits, rather than the entire world [S2, unofficial].
-- **Steps**: Divide the world into chunks. When a dig or build operation modifies the density field, mark only the affected chunks as 'dirty' [S2, unofficial]. In the `LateUpdate` phase of the frame, iterate through dirty chunks and re-mesh them using Marching Cubes [S2, unofficial].
